er paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier"],"id":"short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier","kind":"claim","label":"Theorem D.1 (integer-quotient tests for $`1/21`$)","locator":"Short paper Theorem D.1, p. 20, label res:one-over-twenty-one-frontier","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"*The following statements hold.*\n\n1.  *$1/21\\in\\mathcal A$ if and only if $\\mathcal F_{21}$ does not hold.*\n\n2.  *If there is an unbounded sequence of ranks $R$ with $s_R\\le 2^R$, then $1/21\\in\\mathcal A$.*\n\n3.  *On $\\mathcal F_{21}$, eventually $s_R>2^R$, the boundary rank $R+1$ belongs to $D_{R+1}$, and, for all sufficiently large $R$,\n    ``` math\n    \\begin{aligned}\n     D_{R+1}&=D_R\\cup\\{R+1\\},\\\\\n     s_{R+1}&=4s_R+\n     \\left\\lfloor\\frac{4(2^{2R}\\bmod21)}{21}\\right\\rfloor\n     -2c_{D_R}(2R+1)-c_{D_R}(2R+2)\\\\\n     &\\hspace{3em}{}-(2^{R+1}+1).\n     \\end{aligned}\n    ```\n    Here $c_{D_R}(m)=\\#\\{d\\in D_R:d\\mid m\\}$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.TwentyOneCofinalEvenQuotientGreedyDecay%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22short.res-one-over-twenty-one-frontier%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.TwentyOneCofinalEvenQuotientGreedyDecay%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e485